{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Strange incense</b> — any incense of freewill offering, for all of them are \"strange\" to it except for this one. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 30:9). But Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Exodus 30:9) translated \"incense of foreign spices,\" and did not translate it as נוכריתא (\"foreign\" [in the sense of unauthorized]); he intends to explain that they shall not make incense from spices other than the incense that He will command them, and likewise if one adds other spices to it, one violates this negative prohibition:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:28.904848380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}